  "body": "Add a lollipop cutter tool kind (`ToolKind::Lollipop`) and undercut clearance support so 5-axis finishing operations can machine internal chambers with undercuts cleanly.\n\n### Context\n- Issue #1958 targets internal saxophone mouthpiece chambers that contain undercuts machined with ball-nose and lollipop cutters.\n- `ToolKind` in `crates/tools/src/tools.rs` includes `BallNose` but no `Lollipop` cutter (a spherical cutting head on a narrower neck).\n- `crates/app/src/tool_cutter.rs` narrows only the shank above `flute_len`, and `Flow5D`, `Contour5D`, and `MultiAxisContour` in `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs` admit only `ToolKind::BallNose`.\n\n### Requirements\n- Define `ToolKind::Lollipop` with ball diameter, neck diameter, neck length, and overall reach parameters in `crates/tools`.\n- Admit `ToolKind::Lollipop` in 5-axis finishing operations where valid (`Contour5D`, `Parallel5D`, `Flow5D`, `MultiAxisContour`), and update tool-body collision/shank checks (`avoid.rs`, `tool_body.rs`, `verify`) for the spherical ball plus narrower neck.\n- Ensure gouge and collision laws verify the upper hemisphere of the lollipop cutter on undercut surfaces.\n\nDone means: Users can define a `Lollipop` tool, select it on supported 5-axis finishing operations, generate undercut-safe paths, and detect neck or upper-ball collisions in verification tests.\n\nPart of #1958\n",
